## The idea

A **List** gives O(1) random access ("pick slot 3"), and a **Dictionary** from value → slot gives O(1) lookup. Removing from the middle of a list is normally slow because everything shifts — so instead **move the last element into the hole** and shrink the list by one. Picking a random slot is uniform because the list never has gaps. With duplicates, each value maps to a **set** of slots instead of one.

## Step by step

1. Insert: if the value is already there → false. Otherwise remember its slot (= list length) and append it.
2. Remove: find its slot. Copy the LAST element into that slot and update the last element's slot in the dictionary. Then remove the last list position and the value's dictionary entry.
3. RemoveRandomElement: pick a random slot 0..Count−1, read the value, Remove it. Empty → throw.
4. Multi-bag: value → HashSet of slots. Insert always appends. Remove takes any one slot of the value and does the same "move last into the hole" swap, keeping both values' slot sets correct.

## Worked example

**Input:** Insert 5, 6, 7, then Remove 5

| Step | What happens |
|---|---|
| Insert 5, 6, 7 | list [5, 6, 7]; slots {5:0, 6:1, 7:2} |
| Remove 5 | 5 is at slot 0; last element is 7 |
| move | list[0] = 7; slots[7] = 0 |
| shrink | remove the last position → list [7, 6]; remove 5 from the dictionary |
| state | list [7, 6]; slots {7:0, 6:1} — no shifting needed |

**Result:** [7, 6] — every operation was O(1)

## Cost

Insert, Remove, RemoveRandomElement: O(1) average. Memory O(n).

## The code (C#, compiled and tested against every part of the question)

```csharp
public class RandomBag {
    private readonly List<int> _items = new List<int>();                      // values, no gaps
    private readonly Dictionary<int, int> _slotOf = new Dictionary<int, int>(); // value -> index in _items
    private readonly Random _random;

    public RandomBag(int? seed = null) {
        if (seed.HasValue) _random = new Random(seed.Value);
        else _random = new Random();
    }

    public int Count {
        get { return _items.Count; }
    }

    public bool Insert(int value) {
        if (_slotOf.ContainsKey(value)) return false;       // no duplicates
        _slotOf[value] = _items.Count;
        _items.Add(value);
        return true;
    }

    public bool Remove(int value) {
        int slot;
        if (!_slotOf.TryGetValue(value, out slot)) return false;

        int lastIndex = _items.Count - 1;
        int lastValue = _items[lastIndex];
        _items[slot] = lastValue;          // move the last element into the hole
        _slotOf[lastValue] = slot;         // (safe even when slot == lastIndex)

        _items.RemoveAt(lastIndex);        // removing the LAST position is O(1)
        _slotOf.Remove(value);
        return true;
    }

    public int RemoveRandomElement() {
        if (_items.Count == 0) throw new InvalidOperationException("The bag is empty.");
        int slot = _random.Next(_items.Count);   // uniform because the list has no gaps
        int value = _items[slot];
        Remove(value);
        return value;
    }
}

// Follow-up: duplicates allowed. Each value maps to the SET of slots holding a copy of it.
public class RandomMultiBag {
    private readonly List<int> _items = new List<int>();
    private readonly Dictionary<int, HashSet<int>> _slots = new Dictionary<int, HashSet<int>>();
    private readonly Random _random;

    public RandomMultiBag(int? seed = null) {
        if (seed.HasValue) _random = new Random(seed.Value);
        else _random = new Random();
    }

    public int Count {
        get { return _items.Count; }
    }

    // Always inserts. Returns true if this is the first copy of the value.
    public bool Insert(int value) {
        if (!_slots.ContainsKey(value)) _slots[value] = new HashSet<int>();
        bool firstCopy = _slots[value].Count == 0;
        _slots[value].Add(_items.Count);
        _items.Add(value);
        return firstCopy;
    }

    // Removes ONE copy.
    public bool Remove(int value) {
        HashSet<int> mySlots;
        if (!_slots.TryGetValue(value, out mySlots) || mySlots.Count == 0) return false;

        int slot = -1;
        foreach (int s in mySlots) { slot = s; break; }      // any one copy will do
        int lastIndex = _items.Count - 1;
        int lastValue = _items[lastIndex];

        mySlots.Remove(slot);
        if (slot != lastIndex) {
            _items[slot] = lastValue;                         // move the last element into the hole
            _slots[lastValue].Remove(lastIndex);
            _slots[lastValue].Add(slot);
        }
        _items.RemoveAt(lastIndex);
        if (mySlots.Count == 0) _slots.Remove(value);
        return true;
    }

    public int RemoveRandomElement() {
        if (_items.Count == 0) throw new InvalidOperationException("The bag is empty.");
        int value = _items[_random.Next(_items.Count)];
        Remove(value);
        return value;
    }
}
```

